'''Ritsuko Akagi''' is a [[:Category:Super Rare Cats|Super Rare Cat]] that can be unlocked by playing the [[Cat Capsule#Rare Capsule|Rare Capsule]] during the [[Neon Genesis Evangelion Collaboration Event]]. She was added in [[Version 8.7 Update#Update 8.7.5|Version 8.7.5]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 490
|rarity = SR
|name1 = Ritsuko Akagi
|name2 = First Officer Ritsuko
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''First Officer Ritsuko''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Akagi can find the most usage in [[Into the Future]], sharing similar stats with [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]] as well as also crowd-controlling Alien enemies. Her [[Weaken]] lasts for a good while, though the same can be said about the time she takes to attack. Regardless, use her as you would Surfer and Into the Future will be just the more tolerable.

Once that saga has been beaten, however, Akagi's usefulness starts to drop. Surfer, now with his [[True Form]], Seafarer Cat, finally meets her stats and then some, with guaranteed [[Survive]] and faster attacks that match Akagi's damage output. It is also noted that [[Freeze]] is a far more powerful ability than Weaken. If anything, she can be used as support for Seafarer against the dangerous [[Mesocosmocyclone]], though [[Psychocat (Rare Cat)|Corrupted Psychocat]] already fills that role with the [[Slow]] ability and also Weaken with [[Talents]].

